{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2172-06-01 14:35:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hello, I'm Dr. Lee. I’ll be overseeing your care during this admission. Can you tell me what brought you in today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2172-06-01 14:36:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Hi, Doctor. I’ve been having more frequent low blood sugar episodes—almost daily—and I keep getting confused. I even sent an email to my specialist that I don’t remember writing."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2172-06-01 14:37:25",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That sounds concerning. These episodes—do they come with dizziness, memory loss, or nausea?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2172-06-01 14:38:05",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, all of those. And I’ve been dry heaving a lot, though not actually vomiting. My stomach pain has come back too, like the ulcers I had before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2172-06-01 14:39:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. You're on diazoxide now instead of octreotide, and your tube feeds were adjusted recently. But things aren’t improving?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2172-06-01 14:40:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Right. I was doing well until I came back from my trip. Then the lows started again, and the constipation returned even though I’m eating high-fiber foods."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2172-06-01 14:41:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay. We’ll check your G-tube site, run some labs, and consult neurology and endocrinology. Your symptoms could be tied to hypoglycemia, but we need to rule out other causes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2172-06-01 14:42:40",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will I need any procedures?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2172-06-01 14:43:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Possibly an endoscopy to check for ulcers or other issues in your stomach. But first, we’ll monitor your glucose and adjust your feeds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2172-06-01 16:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your labs came back normal—no infection, liver issues, or electrolyte imbalances. Glucose was 93, which is stable for now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2172-06-01 16:21:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good, but I’m still worried about the lows happening without warning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2172-06-01 16:22:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re going to switch your tube feeding schedule. Instead of continuous, we’ll cycle them—20 during the day, 40 at night—to see if that helps stabilize your sugar."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2172-06-01 16:23:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will that help with the nausea too?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2172-06-01 16:24:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Possibly. We’re also changing your anti-nausea med from Zofran to Compazine, which may work better for you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2172-06-01 18:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Neurology reviewed your case. They don’t think you’re having seizures. Your confusion and memory lapses are likely due to the hypoglycemia."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2172-06-01 18:11:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That makes sense. But how do we stop the lows from happening?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2172-06-01 18:12:35",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll try a monitored fast tomorrow. We’ll stop daytime feeds around 1 PM and check your glucose. If it drops below 55, we’ll draw special labs to understand what’s going on."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2172-06-01 18:13:50",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What if it doesn’t drop?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2172-06-01 18:14:25",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Then we’ll know your body is maintaining sugar okay during fasting, and we can focus on adjusting meds and diet."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2172-06-02 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. How are you feeling? Any symptoms overnight?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2172-06-02 08:01:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No lows, actually. I did have some dry heaving, but not as bad as before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2172-06-02 08:02:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Great. Your fingerstick this morning was 88. We’ll start the fasting study today at 1 PM."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2172-06-02 13:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re stopping your daytime tube feeds now. We’ll check your glucose every 30 minutes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2172-06-02 14:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your glucose is holding at 78. That’s well above the threshold."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2172-06-02 14:31:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So no labs today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2172-06-02 14:32:05",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Correct. But we noticed your glucose meter readings were inconsistent with actual fingersticks. We’ve replaced the meter and strips to ensure accuracy at home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2172-06-02 14:33:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, I didn’t realize it could be off. That might explain some of the scary lows I thought I was having."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2172-06-02 14:34:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. We want you to have reliable tools. We’ll also schedule an endoscopy tomorrow to check your stomach and bypass anatomy."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2172-06-03 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You had the endoscopy this morning. The good news is no ulcers were found at the gastrojejunal anastomosis."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2172-06-03 09:01:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. What about the abnormal mucosa they mentioned?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2172-06-03 09:02:25",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "There are some changes in the esophagus and stomach lining, but nothing urgent. We’ll continue your pantoprazole twice daily to protect the lining."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2172-06-03 09:03:40",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the metronidazole for bacterial overgrowth?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2172-06-03 09:04:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re stopping it for now. The GI team felt it wasn’t clearly helping, and we want to simplify your regimen."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2172-06-03 11:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The nutrition team met with you, right? They went over adding complex carbohydrates by mouth."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2172-06-03 11:01:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, they suggested oatmeal, whole grains—things that digest slowly. I think I can manage that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2172-06-03 11:02:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. That, combined with nighttime tube feeds only, should help prevent rapid glucose swings."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2172-06-03 15:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your glucose has stayed above 78 the entire time. No episodes of hypoglycemia in the hospital."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2172-06-03 15:31:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s really encouraging. Does this mean I can go home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2172-06-03 15:32:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re planning for discharge tomorrow. We’ll finalize your new medication and feeding plan."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2172-06-04 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good news—you’re cleared to go home today. Your mental status is clear, and you’ve been stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2172-06-04 09:01:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What changes should I expect in my routine?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2172-06-04 09:02:25",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll run tube feeds only at night—from 11 PM to 7 AM—at a rate of 40. During the day, you’ll eat complex carbs and avoid simple sugars."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2172-06-04 09:03:40",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my medications?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2172-06-04 09:04:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Diazoxide will now be taken three times a day—25 mg at breakfast, 25 mg at dinner, and 50 mg at bedtime. We’re also switching your sleep med to zolpidem."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2172-06-04 09:05:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What about the nausea?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2172-06-04 09:06:05",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll have prochlorperazine—5 mg up to four times a day as needed. Take it at the first sign of nausea."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2172-06-04 09:07:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And follow-up?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2172-06-04 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll see Dr. ___ in three weeks. Call sooner if you have severe lows, persistent nausea, or confusion."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2172-06-04 09:09:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Doctor. I feel much more confident about managing this now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2172-06-04 09:10:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. We’re here if you need us. Take care, and follow the plan closely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2172-06-04 10:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just a quick check before discharge—your G-tube site looks stable. The hypergranulation tissue is still there, but not infected."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2172-06-04 10:16:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Should I continue the mupirocin?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2172-06-04 10:17:05",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, apply it twice daily as before. If it gets worse, let your surgeon know."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2172-06-04 11:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your discharge paperwork is ready. The nurse will go over everything, including your new feeding schedule and meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2172-06-04 11:31:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll make sure to review it all before I leave."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2172-06-04 12:45:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "One last thing—your mental clarity has improved significantly. That’s likely because your glucose is stabilizing."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2172-06-04 12:46:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I feel more like myself. I hope this continues at home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2172-06-04 12:47:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We do too. Stick to the plan, monitor your sugar with the new meter, and call if anything changes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2172-06-04 14:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The transport team will take you home in about an hour. Do you have any final questions?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2172-06-04 14:21:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, I think I’ve got it all. Thank you for your help."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2172-06-04 14:22:25",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Take care, and we’ll see you at your follow-up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2172-06-04 15:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just confirming—you understand when to take each dose of diazoxide?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2172-06-04 15:01:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes—25 mg with breakfast, 25 mg with dinner, and 50 mg at bedtime."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2172-06-04 15:02:05",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. And remember, the nighttime tube feeds start at 11 PM, rate 40, until 7 AM."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2172-06-04 15:03:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. I’ve written it down to be sure."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2172-06-04 16:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your ride is here. We’re discharging you now. Please follow up as scheduled."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 67,
      "time": "2172-06-04 16:31:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Doctor. I appreciate all your help."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2172-06-01 14:29:00",
    "admission_end": "2172-06-04 19:29:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "The patient was admitted for recurrent hypoglycemia with associated confusion and memory loss, following a recent trip. She reported persistent symptoms despite recent medication changes, including discontinuation of octreotide and initiation of diazoxide. During the hospital stay, her glucose remained stable above 78 mg/dL, and a fasting study was not completed as her levels did not drop below the threshold. An endoscopy showed no acute ulcers but revealed abnormal mucosa in the esophagus and stomach. The metronidazole for bacterial overgrowth was discontinued, and her anti-nausea medication was changed to prochlorperazine. Tube feeds were cycled to nighttime only, and she was transitioned to a complex carbohydrate diet. She was discharged home with a revised diazoxide dosing schedule, nighttime tube feeding protocol, and follow-up planned in three weeks.",
    "problems": [
      "Hypoglycemia, unspecified",
      "Unspecified psychosis",
      "Memory loss",
      "Constipation, unspecified",
      "Bariatric surgery status",
      "Esophageal reflux",
      "Depressive disorder, not elsewhere classified",
      "Anxiety state, unspecified",
      "Family history of ischemic heart disease",
      "Gastrostomy status"
    ]
  }
}
